From a2b2ab25cec10d8a87de8458f32fc6c2316bb505 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:14:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] cuda : 128-row tiles in the sm_60 expert GEMM for wide
 token tiles

With 64 pairs per tile, a block now takes 128 rows (8 per thread instead of 4): half the weight-side shared-memory
loads per HFMA2. Same per-output summation order: results unchanged. 1536 tokens, 256 experts x 8 used: q4_K gate
6.9 -> 7.1 TFLOPS, q5_K down 6.8 -> 7.1 TFLOPS. 2x P100 pp4096 1578 -> 1592 t/s.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
